  {
    "@id": "https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/laura-secords-thing#202705222000",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/additionalType": [
      {
        "@id": "http://kg.artsdata.ca/resource/TheatrePerformance"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Canada’s patron saint of being misremembered.\n\nFrom the original mind of Brad Gira comes a campy, high-stakes comedy that reimagines the legendary 20-mile (or 32-kilometre) trek of Canadian folk hero Laura Secord.\n\nSecord’s journey helped thwart an American attack during the War of 1812, though it was largely ignored during her lifetime – and many now only know her as a chocolate brand. This comedy pokes at a story we thought was settled – revealing the human pulse beneath the legend and reminding us that even our most fixed histories began as acts of risk.\n\nWith wit and irreverence, Laura Secord’s Thing unpacks myth, memory, and the farcical spectre of national storytelling."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
