  {
    "@id": "https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/the-ghosts-of-mariupol#202704202000",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/additionalType": [
      {
        "@id": "http://kg.artsdata.ca/resource/TheatrePerformance"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Theatre in the aftermath of catastrophe.\n\nAs Ukraine enters the fifth year of Russia’s ongoing invasion, Christopher Morris presents a powerful new work inspired by the artists who survived the March 2022 bombing of Ukraine’s historic Donetsk Academic Regional Drama Theatre in Mariupol.\n\nThe play follows two actresses, best friends whose lives are forever changed by the bombing. One collaborates with Russians in the rebuilt Mariupol Theatre. The other creates theatre for injured Ukrainian soldiers in Western Ukraine. Both are haunted by the choices they made that day to survive.\n\nThe Ghosts of Mariupol confronts impossible questions about survival, collaboration, truth, and resistance. It asks: when war shatters moral clarity, what’s the true cost of survival? And how do you hold on to yourself when war has changed you forever?"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.crowstheatre.com/uploads/2026.27%20Season/09%20THE%20GHOSTS%20OF%20MARIUPOL/GHO_2400x1350_centre_.jpg#ImageObject"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.crowstheatre.com/about/our-venues#studio-theatre"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Ghosts of Mariupol"
      }
    ],
